From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:37:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 365/368] tools/asahi: test the T8132 deep sleep enable guard

Check that S3_5_C15_C6_2 is written in one place only, inside the
dse_allowed() guard; that the guard follows apple_cpu.t8132_dse (0 auto,
1 never, 2 always, nothing above 2, a log line at 2) and otherwise the
boot flag, which only aura's mailbox branch sets, from its execute
window property; that the stub without CPU hotplug says no; and that
apple-s2r refuses a real T8132 sleep with -EOPNOTSUPP and one line,
after the read-only checks and before any watchdog, crumb, coprocessor
stop or core stop. Runs that abort before the commit are not refused.

For the EFI stub, check that the window property must be two u64s,
that the check runs only after the Image is placed and never changes
the status, and run its containment test with u64 arithmetic, wrap
cases included. Each check has a mutation that must fail it.

Assisted-by: LLM
